IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lsl-dates`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1955 (NSW) -- the rules a worker (or a worker's personal representative) meets in claiming
-- long service leave or pay for it: who is a worker and who is left out (s 3, s 5), continuous service and the breaks
-- that do and do not count (s 4(11), (13), s 15C), the amount of leave (s 4(2)), ordinary pay (s 3), taking the leave
-- (s 4(3)-(3B), (4A), (10), (10A)), payment on termination or death and the deduction for leave taken in advance
-- (s 4(5), (5AA)-(5B), (8), (9)), the employer's records (s 8(3)), penalties (s 10, s 10A, s 11) and the 6-year window
-- for recovering pay (s 12).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in lsl-seat.l4 (the worker), which IMPORTs it and restates no
-- rule. Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS are named outcomes (enumerations), dates or numbers, never MAYBE BOOLEAN, so no NOTHING-kind tag is used.
-- Where the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, "only if", "shall not", a closed list of reasons) the
-- outcome begins "no:"; where a provision's scope is not met without an "only" the outcome says the provision "does not
-- reach this". Judgments the Act leaves to someone else (serious and wilful misconduct, a bona fide bailment, the
-- needs of the employer's establishment) are inputs: the answer is conditional on them, never a guess at them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website at 10 March 2025, via the Open Australian
-- Legal Corpus (version as at 1 July 2024). State of New South Wales, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE
-- ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Long Service Leave Act 1955`

§§ `s 3 and s 5 -- who the Act gives long service leave to`

-- s 3(1): "Worker means person employed, whether on salary or wages or piecework rates, or as a member of a buttygang"
-- (commission, labour-only contracts, outworkers and the like do not "in itself prevent" a person being a worker),
-- "but does not include a person who is a worker within the meaning of the Long Service Leave (Metalliferous Mining
-- Industry) Act 1963". s 3(3): a bailee driver of a vehicle or vessel, in work for which an award or industrial
-- agreement fixes a rate, is deemed a worker of the bailor "unless ... [it is] establishe[d] to the satisfaction of the
-- tribunal ... that the contract of bailment was a bona fide contract and was not entered into for the purpose of
-- avoiding the operation of this Act". s 3(4): a person deemed an employee by the Industrial Relations Act 1996 is
-- deemed a worker. Whether a person is "employed" is borrowed and asked as a fact.
DECLARE `How I work` IS ONE OF
    `I am employed by the employer, on salary, wages, piecework or commission, or as an outworker or under a labour-only contract`
    `I ply for hire, deliver goods or carry passengers in a vehicle or vessel bailed to me by the other person, in work for which an award or industrial agreement fixes a rate`
    `I am deemed an employee of the other person by the Industrial Relations Act 1996`
    `I am not employed: I work on my own account`

-- s 5(2)(a): the Industrial Relations Commission may exempt an employer whose scheme is not less favourable; s 5(2)(c)(i):
-- the exemption "shall not apply ... in respect of any worker who, within a period of three months after the date from
-- which the exemption takes effect, or the date of commencement of the worker's employment, as the case may require,
-- has by notice in writing to the employer elected to be subject to the provisions of this Act".
DECLARE `Exemption status` IS ONE OF
    `my employer has no exemption from the Industrial Relations Commission`
    `my employer has an exemption under s 5(2) and I elected in writing, in time, to come under this Act`
    `my employer has an exemption under s 5(2) and I did not elect to come under this Act`

DECLARE `Coverage answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you are a worker, and s 4 entitles you to long service leave on ordinary pay for your service with the employer (s 3(1), s 4(1))`
    `no: a worker means a person employed (s 3(1)), and you are not employed, so the Act gives you no long service leave`
    `no: the tribunal was satisfied that the bailment was bona fide and not made to avoid the Act, so you are not deemed a worker (s 3(3))`
    `no: a person who is a worker under the Long Service Leave (Metalliferous Mining Industry) Act 1963 is not a worker under this Act (s 3(1))`
    `no: s 4 does not apply to you because your award or agreement gives long service leave more favourable than s 4; you take it under the award or agreement (s 5(1)(a))`
    `no: s 4 does not apply to you because another Act provides long service leave for your class of workers (s 5(1)(b))`
    `no: your employer is exempt from the Act's long service leave provisions for you, and its scheme applies instead (s 5(2)(a), (c))`

GIVEN `how I work` IS A `How I work`
      `the tribunal is satisfied the bailment is bona fide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am a worker under the metalliferous mining Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my award or agreement gives more favourable long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another Act gives my class of workers long service leave` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exemption status` IS AN `Exemption status`
GIVETH A `Coverage answer`
`the coverage answer for` `how I work` `bailment bona fide` `the tribunal is satisfied the bailment is bona fide` `metalliferous` `I am a worker under the metalliferous mining Act` `award` `my award or agreement gives more favourable long service leave` `other Act` `another Act gives my class of workers long service leave` `exemption` `the exemption status` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `how I work` EQUALS `I am not employed: I work on my own account`
        THEN `no: a worker means a person employed (s 3(1)), and you are not employed, so the Act gives you no long service leave`
        IF     `how I work` EQUALS `I ply for hire, deliver goods or carry passengers in a vehicle or vessel bailed to me by the other person, in work for which an award or industrial agreement fixes a rate`
           AND `the tribunal is satisfied the bailment is bona fide`
        THEN `no: the tribunal was satisfied that the bailment was bona fide and not made to avoid the Act, so you are not deemed a worker (s 3(3))`
        IF `I am a worker under the metalliferous mining Act`
        THEN `no: a person who is a worker under the Long Service Leave (Metalliferous Mining Industry) Act 1963 is not a worker under this Act (s 3(1))`
        IF `my award or agreement gives more favourable long service leave`
        THEN `no: s 4 does not apply to you because your award or agreement gives long service leave more favourable than s 4; you take it under the award or agreement (s 5(1)(a))`
        IF `another Act gives my class of workers long service leave`
        THEN `no: s 4 does not apply to you because another Act provides long service leave for your class of workers (s 5(1)(b))`
        IF `the exemption status` EQUALS `my employer has an exemption under s 5(2) and I did not elect to come under this Act`
        THEN `no: your employer is exempt from the Act's long service leave provisions for you, and its scheme applies instead (s 5(2)(a), (c))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you are a worker, and s 4 entitles you to long service leave on ordinary pay for your service with the employer (s 3(1), s 4(1))`

-- s 5(2)(c)(i): the election must be made "within a period of three months after the date from which the exemption
-- takes effect, or the date of commencement of the worker's employment, as the case may require": read as the later of
-- the two (a worker already employed counts from the exemption; one employed later, from the start of employment), and
-- the last day as the same day of the month 3 months later (fork F1, F9).
GIVEN `the day the exemption took effect` IS A DATE, `the day my employment began` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to elect out of an exempt scheme` `the day the exemption took effect` `the day my employment began` MEANS
    (`the later of` `the day the exemption took effect` `and` `the day my employment began`) `plus months` 3

§§ `s 4(11), s 4(13), s 15C -- continuous service, and breaks`

-- s 4(11)(a): "service of a worker with an employer means continuous service, whether on a permanent, casual,
-- part-time or any other basis, under one or more contracts of employment". (a1): service is deemed continuous despite
-- a break "by reason only of" (i) absence under the terms of employment, (ii) illness or injury, (iii) an employer's
-- termination to avoid obligations, (iv) an industrial dispute, (v) slackness of trade, (vi) absence by leave of the
-- employer, (vii) any other termination by the employer where the worker returns "within 2 months"; "but the period
-- during which the service is so interrupted or determined shall not in the circumstances referred to in
-- subparagraphs (iii)-(vii) ... be taken into account in calculating the period of service" (fork F3: the days of a
-- break under (i) or (ii) count). (b) and (13)(d): an apprenticeship counts where the contract of employment is made
-- "within a period of twelve months after the completion" of it. (c): a business transmitted to a new employer. (13)(b)
-- (ii), (c): a transfer to a related corporation, "only if ... within a period of two months after the termination".
-- s 15C: a stand-down without pay because of COVID-19 during the prescribed period.
DECLARE `Kind of break` IS ONE OF
    `an absence under the terms of my employment, such as paid leave`
    `an absence because of my illness or injury`
    `my employer ended or interrupted my service to avoid long service leave or sick leave obligations`
    `an industrial dispute`
    `my employer ended or interrupted my service because of slackness of trade`
    `an absence for any cause with my employer's leave`
    `my employer ended or interrupted my service for another reason`
    `I resigned, or left for a reason of my own, and later came back`
    `I was stood down without pay because of the COVID-19 pandemic`
    `the business I worked in was transferred to a new employer, and I went with it`
    `I moved to a corporation related to my employer (its holding company, its subsidiary, or another subsidiary of its holding company)`
    `I had finished an apprenticeship with this employer, or with a corporation related to it`

DECLARE `Continuity answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes, continuous, and the time counts as service: the break was an absence under the terms of your employment or because of illness or injury (s 4(11)(a1)(i), (ii))`
    `yes, continuous, but the days of the break are not counted as service (s 4(11)(a1)(iii)-(vi))` HAS `days not counted` IS A NUMBER
    `yes, continuous, because you came back within 2 months; the days of the break are not counted as service (s 4(11)(a1)(vii))` HAS `days not counted` IS A NUMBER
    `no: you came back more than 2 months after your employer ended your service, so service before the break is not continuous with service after it (s 4(11)(a), (a1)(vii))`
    `no: service means continuous service (s 4(11)(a)), and leaving of your own accord is not one of the breaks the Act saves, so service before the break does not count`
    `yes, continuous, and the time counts: you were stood down without pay because of COVID-19 during the prescribed period, and you kept accruing long service leave (s 15C(1))`
    `s 15C does not reach this: the stand-down began outside the prescribed period (11 March 2020 to 30 September 2021, unless a regulation prescribed a later day, not after 31 March 2022); see whether a head of s 4(11)(a1) applies`
    `yes, continuous, and your service with the old employer counts as service with the new one (s 4(11)(c))`
    `yes, continuous, and your service with the first corporation counts as service with the related one, because the new contract was made within 2 months after the first one ended; the days between are not counted (s 4(13)(b)(ii), (c))` HAS `days not counted` IS A NUMBER
    `no: a move to a related corporation keeps your service only if the new contract was made within 2 months after the first one ended (s 4(13)(b)(ii))`
    `yes, your apprenticeship counts as service, because you entered the contract of employment within 12 months after completing it; the days between are not counted (s 4(11)(b), s 4(13)(d))` HAS `days not counted` IS A NUMBER
    `no: the apprenticeship counts only if you entered the contract of employment within 12 months after completing it (s 4(11)(b), s 4(13)(d))`

-- s 15C(3): the prescribed period starts on 11 March 2020 and ends on 30 September 2021 or a later day, not later than
-- 31 March 2022, prescribed by the regulations. No regulation is deposited, so the Act's own 30 September 2021 is used
-- (finding 4); a stand-down counts if it began within the period (fork F4).
`the first day of the COVID-19 period` MEANS `the date` 11 3 2020
`the last day of the COVID-19 period` MEANS `the date` 30 9 2021

-- One break. "The day it began" is the first day off work (for an apprenticeship or a move between corporations, the
-- day after the earlier engagement ended); "the day I came back" is the first day of service again. The days not
-- counted run from the first to the second (fork F5: the day of return is service).
GIVEN `the kind of break` IS A `Kind of break`
      `the day it began` IS A DATE
      `the day I came back` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Continuity answer`
`the continuity answer for` `the kind of break` `from` `the day it began` `back on` `the day I came back` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of break`
    WHEN `an absence under the terms of my employment, such as paid leave` THEN `yes, continuous, and the time counts as service: the break was an absence under the terms of your employment or because of illness or injury (s 4(11)(a1)(i), (ii))`
    WHEN `an absence because of my illness or injury` THEN `yes, continuous, and the time counts as service: the break was an absence under the terms of your employment or because of illness or injury (s 4(11)(a1)(i), (ii))`
    WHEN `my employer ended or interrupted my service to avoid long service leave or sick leave obligations` THEN `yes, continuous, but the days of the break are not counted as service (s 4(11)(a1)(iii)-(vi))` `the length`
    WHEN `an industrial dispute` THEN `yes, continuous, but the days of the break are not counted as service (s 4(11)(a1)(iii)-(vi))` `the length`
    WHEN `my employer ended or interrupted my service because of slackness of trade` THEN `yes, continuous, but the days of the break are not counted as service (s 4(11)(a1)(iii)-(vi))` `the length`
    WHEN `an absence for any cause with my employer's leave` THEN `yes, continuous, but the days of the break are not counted as service (s 4(11)(a1)(iii)-(vi))` `the length`
    WHEN `my employer ended or interrupted my service for another reason` THEN
        IF `the day I came back` `is on or before` (`the day it began` `plus months` 2)
        THEN `yes, continuous, because you came back within 2 months; the days of the break are not counted as service (s 4(11)(a1)(vii))` `the length`
        ELSE `no: you came back more than 2 months after your employer ended your service, so service before the break is not continuous with service after it (s 4(11)(a), (a1)(vii))`
    WHEN `I resigned, or left for a reason of my own, and later came back` THEN `no: service means continuous service (s 4(11)(a)), and leaving of your own accord is not one of the breaks the Act saves, so service before the break does not count`
    WHEN `I was stood down without pay because of the COVID-19 pandemic` THEN
        IF     `the first day of the COVID-19 period` `is on or before` `the day it began`
           AND `the day it began` `is on or before` `the last day of the COVID-19 period`
        THEN `yes, continuous, and the time counts: you were stood down without pay because of COVID-19 during the prescribed period, and you kept accruing long service leave (s 15C(1))`
        ELSE `s 15C does not reach this: the stand-down began outside the prescribed period (11 March 2020 to 30 September 2021, unless a regulation prescribed a later day, not after 31 March 2022); see whether a head of s 4(11)(a1) applies`
    WHEN `the business I worked in was transferred to a new employer, and I went with it` THEN `yes, continuous, and your service with the old employer counts as service with the new one (s 4(11)(c))`
    WHEN `I moved to a corporation related to my employer (its holding company, its subsidiary, or another subsidiary of its holding company)` THEN
        IF `the day I came back` `is on or before` (`the day it began` `plus months` 2)
        THEN `yes, continuous, and your service with the first corporation counts as service with the related one, because the new contract was made within 2 months after the first one ended; the days between are not counted (s 4(13)(b)(ii), (c))` `the length`
        ELSE `no: a move to a related corporation keeps your service only if the new contract was made within 2 months after the first one ended (s 4(13)(b)(ii))`
    WHEN `I had finished an apprenticeship with this employer, or with a corporation related to it` THEN
        IF `the day I came back` `is on or before` (`the day it began` `plus months` 12)
        THEN `yes, your apprenticeship counts as service, because you entered the contract of employment within 12 months after completing it; the days between are not counted (s 4(11)(b), s 4(13)(d))` `the length`
        ELSE `no: the apprenticeship counts only if you entered the contract of employment within 12 months after completing it (s 4(11)(b), s 4(13)(d))`
    WHERE
        `the length` MEANS `the larger of` 0 `and` (`the days from` `the day it began` `to` `the day I came back`)

§§ `s 4(2) -- how much long service leave`

-- s 4(13)(e): a worker who transfers to a related corporation is not terminated for s 4(2) and (5). s 4(2)(a)(iii):
-- five to ten years count only where the services "are terminated by the employer for any reason other than the
-- worker's serious and wilful misconduct, or by the worker on account of illness, incapacity or domestic or other
-- pressing necessity, or by reason of the death of the worker". Misconduct and necessity are judgments, asked as
-- facts.
DECLARE `How my employment ended` IS ONE OF
    `it has not ended: I am still employed`
    `I moved to a corporation related to my employer, which is not a termination`
    `my employer terminated it, other than for serious and wilful misconduct`
    `my employer terminated it for serious and wilful misconduct`
    `I ended it because of illness, incapacity, or domestic or other pressing necessity`
    `I ended it for another reason`
    `I died`
    `it ended in another way, such as the end of a fixed term`

-- One employment with one employer. "The last day of service" is the last day employed (or, while still employed, the
-- day asked about). Days not counted are those left out by s 4(11)(a1) and the like; they move the start forward
-- (fork F2).
DECLARE `Service facts` HAS
    `the day service began`       IS A DATE
    `the last day of service`     IS A DATE
    `days not counted`            IS A NUMBER
    `how it ended`                IS A `How my employment ended`
    `weeks already taken or paid` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the counted start of` f MEANS (f's `the day service began`) `plus days` (f's `days not counted`)

GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day after service of` f MEANS (f's `the last day of service`) `plus days` 1

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`anniversary` n `of` f MEANS (`the counted start of` f) `plus months` (12 TIMES n)

-- Completed years: n years are completed when the day after the last day of service is on or after the nth
-- anniversary of the counted start (fork F2).
GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the completed years of` f MEANS
    `the larger of` 0 `and` (IF (`anniversary` `the year guess` `of` f) `is on or before` (`the day after service of` f) THEN `the year guess` ELSE `the year guess` MINUS 1)
    WHERE
        `the year guess` MEANS DATE_YEAR (`the day after service of` f) MINUS DATE_YEAR (`the counted start of` f)

-- Service in years, with the part year as a fraction of the days in that service year (fork F2).
GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the service in years of` f MEANS
    `the completed years of` f PLUS (`the part days` DIVIDED BY `the days in that year`)
    WHERE
        `the part days`        MEANS `the days from` (`anniversary` (`the completed years of` f) `of` f) `to` (`the day after service of` f)
        `the days in that year` MEANS `the days from` (`anniversary` (`the completed years of` f) `of` f) `to` (`anniversary` ((`the completed years of` f) PLUS 1) `of` f)

GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the services are terminated for` f IF
    NOT (   f's `how it ended` EQUALS `it has not ended: I am still employed`
         OR f's `how it ended` EQUALS `I moved to a corporation related to my employer, which is not a termination`)

GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a s 4(2)(a)(iii) reason holds for` f IF
        f's `how it ended` EQUALS `my employer terminated it, other than for serious and wilful misconduct`
    OR  f's `how it ended` EQUALS `I ended it because of illness, incapacity, or domestic or other pressing necessity`
    OR  f's `how it ended` EQUALS `I died`

-- s 4(2)(a)(i)(A), (B): 2 months for 10 years, and 1 month for each 5 years completed since last entitled.
GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months accrued in service for` f MEANS
    IF `the completed years of` f AT LEAST 10
    THEN 2 PLUS FLOOR ((`the completed years of` f MINUS 10) DIVIDED BY 5)
    ELSE 0

-- s 4(2)(a)(i)(C): the years "completed since the worker last became entitled": the last entitlement came at 10 years
-- plus each complete 5 years after.
GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the completed years since last entitled for` f MEANS
    `the completed years of` f MINUS (10 PLUS (5 TIMES FLOOR ((`the completed years of` f MINUS 10) DIVIDED BY 5)))

-- s 4(2)(a): the amount, in months. (i)(C) on termination after 15 years: whole completed years since last entitled
-- at 2 months for 10 years (fork F6, finding 2). (ii) 10 to 15 years, terminated or ceasing for any reason:
-- 3 months for 15 years on the actual service (read as the whole amount, (i)(A)'s 2 months within it: fork F7).
-- (iii) 5 to 10 years, terminated for a listed reason: 2 months for 10 years on the actual service. (a2), service
-- before 1963, is out of scope.
GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months of long service leave for` f MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the services are terminated for` f)
        THEN `the months accrued in service for` f
        IF `the completed years of` f AT LEAST 15
        THEN `the months accrued in service for` f PLUS ((`the completed years since last entitled for` f) TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 10)
        IF `the completed years of` f AT LEAST 10
        THEN (`the service in years of` f) TIMES 3 DIVIDED BY 15
        IF `the completed years of` f AT LEAST 5 AND `a s 4(2)(a)(iii) reason holds for` f
        THEN (`the service in years of` f) TIMES 2 DIVIDED BY 10
        OTHERWISE 0

-- s 4(2)(a3): "month means 4 and one-third weeks".
`weeks in a month` MEANS 13 DIVIDED BY 3

GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weeks of long service leave for` f MEANS (`the months of long service leave for` f) TIMES `weeks in a month`

-- s 4(2)(b)(ii), s 4(3) proviso, s 4(5)(a): leave already taken or paid for (other than leave under an agreement for
-- leave in addition to the Act's) comes off.
GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weeks still owed for` f MEANS `the larger of` 0 `and` ((`the weeks of long service leave for` f) MINUS (f's `weeks already taken or paid`))

-- s 4(2)(a)(i)(A): the worker becomes entitled on completing 10 years service: the 10th anniversary of the counted
-- start (fork F2).
GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day first entitled for` f MEANS `anniversary` 10 `of` f

§§ `s 3 -- ordinary pay`

-- s 3(2)(d): board and lodging at the value fixed by the terms of employment, otherwise $15 a week for board and $5 a
-- week for lodging, "or such greater sum as may be prescribed instead" (no regulation deposited: finding 4).
DECLARE `Board or lodging` IS ONE OF
    `not provided`
    `provided, with a cash value fixed by the terms of my employment`
    `provided, with no cash value fixed`

DECLARE `Pay facts` HAS
    `paid wholly at an ordinary time rate`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `weekly ordinary remuneration now`               IS A NUMBER
    `average weekly ordinary remuneration, 5 years`  IS A NUMBER
    `average weekly wage, 12 months`                 IS A NUMBER
    `average weekly wage, 5 years`                   IS A NUMBER
    `average weekly bonuses, 12 months`              IS A NUMBER
    `average weekly bonuses, 5 years`                IS A NUMBER
    `board`                                          IS A `Board or lodging`
    `fixed weekly value of board`                    IS A NUMBER
    `lodging`                                        IS A `Board or lodging`
    `fixed weekly value of lodging`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the s 3(2C) annual amount`                      IS A NUMBER

-- s 3(1)(a), (b): the greater of the two; on a tie the first (12 months, or the rate now) is taken (fork F8).
GIVEN p IS A `Pay facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shorter period is used for` p IF
    IF p's `paid wholly at an ordinary time rate`
    THEN p's `weekly ordinary remuneration now` AT LEAST p's `average weekly ordinary remuneration, 5 years`
    ELSE p's `average weekly wage, 12 months` AT LEAST p's `average weekly wage, 5 years`

GIVEN p IS A `Pay facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the base weekly pay for` p MEANS
    IF p's `paid wholly at an ordinary time rate`
    THEN `the larger of` (p's `weekly ordinary remuneration now`) `and` (p's `average weekly ordinary remuneration, 5 years`)
    ELSE `the larger of` (p's `average weekly wage, 12 months`) `and` (p's `average weekly wage, 5 years`)

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Board or lodging`, `the fixed value` IS A NUMBER, `the Act's value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cash value of` `the kind` `fixed at` `the fixed value` `or else` `the Act's value` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `not provided` THEN 0
    WHEN `provided, with a cash value fixed by the terms of my employment` THEN `the fixed value`
    WHEN `provided, with no cash value fixed` THEN `the Act's value`

GIVEN p IS A `Pay facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the board and lodging for` p MEANS
    (`the cash value of` (p's `board`) `fixed at` (p's `fixed weekly value of board`) `or else` 15)
    PLUS (`the cash value of` (p's `lodging`) `fixed at` (p's `fixed weekly value of lodging`) `or else` 5)

-- s 3(2C): bonuses are left out "if the annual amount of the worker's ordinary pay (excluding any amounts so paid)
-- exceeds the amount prescribed by the regulations"; the annual amount is read as 52 weeks (fork F8).
GIVEN p IS A `Pay facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bonuses are left out for` p IF
    ((`the base weekly pay for` p) PLUS (`the board and lodging for` p)) TIMES 52 GREATER THAN p's `the s 3(2C) annual amount`

GIVEN p IS A `Pay facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the bonuses for` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `bonuses are left out for` p THEN 0
        IF `the shorter period is used for` p THEN p's `average weekly bonuses, 12 months`
        OTHERWISE p's `average weekly bonuses, 5 years`

GIVEN p IS A `Pay facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly ordinary pay for` p MEANS
    (`the base weekly pay for` p) PLUS (`the bonuses for` p) PLUS (`the board and lodging for` p)

§§ `s 4(3)-(3B), (4A), (10), (10A) -- taking the leave`

DECLARE `How I want to take the leave` IS ONE OF
    `in one continuous period`
    `in two or more separate periods`
    `in advance, before I am entitled to it`
    `from a later date agreed with my employer`

DECLARE `Taking leave answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the leave is given and taken in one continuous period, as soon as practicable having regard to the needs of the employer's establishment (s 4(3)(a), (b))`
    `yes: with your employer's agreement you may take it in two or more separate periods, each of at least 1 day (s 4(3)(b), (3AA))`
    `no: separate periods need your employer's agreement; otherwise the leave is taken in one continuous period (s 4(3)(b), (3AA))`
    `no: each period must be at least 1 day (s 4(3AA), (3A)); for a worker with no fixed weekly hours a day is worked out under s 4(3B)`
    `yes: with your employer's agreement you may take a period of at least 1 day in advance; on termination your employer may deduct pay for leave taken beyond your entitlement (s 4(3A), (5)(c))`
    `no: leave in advance needs your employer's agreement (s 4(3A))`
    `yes: you and your employer have agreed to postpone the leave, so it is taken from the agreed date (s 4(3)(a)); you may also agree that your ordinary pay is fixed as at the date of that agreement (s 3(2B))`
    `no: postponing the leave needs an agreement with your employer; otherwise it is given and taken as soon as practicable (s 4(3)(a))`

GIVEN `the way` IS A `How I want to take the leave`
      `my employer agrees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shortest period in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Taking leave answer`
`the taking leave answer for` `the way` `agreed` `my employer agrees` `shortest` `the shortest period in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way`
    WHEN `in one continuous period` THEN `yes: the leave is given and taken in one continuous period, as soon as practicable having regard to the needs of the employer's establishment (s 4(3)(a), (b))`
    WHEN `in two or more separate periods` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF NOT `my employer agrees` THEN `no: separate periods need your employer's agreement; otherwise the leave is taken in one continuous period (s 4(3)(b), (3AA))`
            IF `the shortest period in days` LESS THAN 1 THEN `no: each period must be at least 1 day (s 4(3AA), (3A)); for a worker with no fixed weekly hours a day is worked out under s 4(3B)`
            OTHERWISE `yes: with your employer's agreement you may take it in two or more separate periods, each of at least 1 day (s 4(3)(b), (3AA))`
    WHEN `in advance, before I am entitled to it` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF NOT `my employer agrees` THEN `no: leave in advance needs your employer's agreement (s 4(3A))`
            IF `the shortest period in days` LESS THAN 1 THEN `no: each period must be at least 1 day (s 4(3AA), (3A)); for a worker with no fixed weekly hours a day is worked out under s 4(3B)`
            OTHERWISE `yes: with your employer's agreement you may take a period of at least 1 day in advance; on termination your employer may deduct pay for leave taken beyond your entitlement (s 4(3A), (5)(c))`
    WHEN `from a later date agreed with my employer` THEN
        IF `my employer agrees`
        THEN `yes: you and your employer have agreed to postpone the leave, so it is taken from the agreed date (s 4(3)(a)); you may also agree that your ordinary pay is fixed as at the date of that agreement (s 3(2B))`
        ELSE `no: postponing the leave needs an agreement with your employer; otherwise it is given and taken as soon as practicable (s 4(3)(a))`

-- s 4(3B): for a worker with no fixed normal weekly hours, "1 day" is a number of hours "calculated as follows" -- the
-- formula is missing from the deposited text (finding 3) -- "where A is the higher of" the average weekly hours over
-- 12 months and over 5 years ending the day before the leave, "and B is the average number of days worked weekly ...
-- during the period used for calculating A". Read as A divided by B (fork F10); on a tie, the 12 months.
GIVEN `weekly hours, 12 months` IS A NUMBER, `weekly hours, 5 years` IS A NUMBER, `days a week, 12 months` IS A NUMBER, `days a week, 5 years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours in a day of leave for` `weekly hours, 12 months` `and` `weekly hours, 5 years` `working` `days a week, 12 months` `or` `days a week, 5 years` MEANS
    IF `weekly hours, 12 months` AT LEAST `weekly hours, 5 years`
    THEN `weekly hours, 12 months` DIVIDED BY `days a week, 12 months`
    ELSE `weekly hours, 5 years` DIVIDED BY `days a week, 5 years`

-- s 4(4A): a Governor's public holiday for the whole State, falling in the leave, on which the worker is entitled to
-- payment, adds one day.
GIVEN `public holidays in the leave` IS A NUMBER, `I am entitled to payment for them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the extra days for` `public holidays in the leave` `paid` `I am entitled to payment for them` MEANS
    IF `I am entitled to payment for them` THEN `the larger of` 0 `and` `public holidays in the leave` ELSE 0

-- s 4(10): "at least one month's notice of the date from which it is proposed that the worker's long service leave
-- shall be given and taken"; (10A): less if the worker agrees. The last day for notice is one month before the leave
-- begins (fork F1, F11).
GIVEN `the day the leave begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for notice of leave beginning` `the day the leave begins` MEANS `the day the leave begins` `plus months` (0 MINUS 1)

DECLARE `Notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: you were given at least one month's notice of the date your leave begins (s 4(10))`
    `yes: you were given less than one month's notice, but you agreed to the shorter notice (s 4(10A))`
    `no: your employer had to give you at least one month's notice of the date your leave begins, that is by the day shown, unless you agreed to less (s 4(10), (10A))` HAS `the last day for notice` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the day the leave begins` IS A DATE, `the day notice was given` IS A DATE, `I agreed to less notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`the notice answer for leave beginning` `the day the leave begins` `notified on` `the day notice was given` `agreed` `I agreed to less notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day notice was given` `is on or before` (`the last day for notice of leave beginning` `the day the leave begins`)
        THEN `yes: you were given at least one month's notice of the date your leave begins (s 4(10))`
        IF `I agreed to less notice`
        THEN `yes: you were given less than one month's notice, but you agreed to the shorter notice (s 4(10A))`
        OTHERWISE `no: your employer had to give you at least one month's notice of the date your leave begins, that is by the day shown, unless you agreed to less (s 4(10), (10A))` (`the last day for notice of leave beginning` `the day the leave begins`)

§§ `s 4(5), (5AA)-(5B), (8), (9) -- payment instead of leave, on termination and on death`

DECLARE `Payment answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: while you are employed, your employer must not pay you instead of giving you the leave, and you must not accept such a payment; no agreement can change that (s 4(8), s 7)`
    `no: a move to a related corporation is not a termination (s 4(13)(e)); your service carries over and the leave is still to be taken, not paid out (s 4(8))`
    `yes: you are taken to have begun the leave on the day your employment ended, and your employer must forthwith pay you in full your ordinary pay for the untaken leave, less anything already paid for it (s 4(5)(a))`
    `yes, to your personal representative: on the personal representative's request the employer must pay in full the ordinary pay for the untaken leave, less anything already paid for it (s 4(5)(b)); the personal representative may recover it as you could (s 4(9))`
    `not yet: you are registered under a portable long service scheme for building or contract cleaning workers, so your employer must not give you leave or pay you for it unless you apply (s 4(5A), (5B))`

GIVEN `how it ended` IS A `How my employment ended`
      `I am a registered portable scheme worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have applied to my employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
`the payment answer for` `how it ended` `registered` `I am a registered portable scheme worker` `applied` `I have applied to my employer` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `how it ended` EQUALS `it has not ended: I am still employed`
        THEN `no: while you are employed, your employer must not pay you instead of giving you the leave, and you must not accept such a payment; no agreement can change that (s 4(8), s 7)`
        IF `how it ended` EQUALS `I moved to a corporation related to my employer, which is not a termination`
        THEN `no: a move to a related corporation is not a termination (s 4(13)(e)); your service carries over and the leave is still to be taken, not paid out (s 4(8))`
        IF `I am a registered portable scheme worker` AND NOT `I have applied to my employer`
        THEN `not yet: you are registered under a portable long service scheme for building or contract cleaning workers, so your employer must not give you leave or pay you for it unless you apply (s 4(5A), (5B))`
        IF `how it ended` EQUALS `I died`
        THEN `yes, to your personal representative: on the personal representative's request the employer must pay in full the ordinary pay for the untaken leave, less anything already paid for it (s 4(5)(b)); the personal representative may recover it as you could (s 4(9))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: you are taken to have begun the leave on the day your employment ended, and your employer must forthwith pay you in full your ordinary pay for the untaken leave, less anything already paid for it (s 4(5)(a))`

-- s 4(5)(a), (b): the ordinary pay for the untaken leave "less any amount already paid ... in respect of that leave".
-- While employed (or on a move to a related corporation) nothing is payable (s 4(8)).
GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`, `weekly ordinary pay` IS A NUMBER, `already paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the termination payment for` f `at` `weekly ordinary pay` `less` `already paid` MEANS
    IF `the services are terminated for` f
    THEN `the larger of` 0 `and` (((`the weeks still owed for` f) TIMES `weekly ordinary pay`) MINUS `already paid`)
    ELSE 0

-- s 4(5)(c): on termination, for leave taken in advance under s 4(3A), the employer "may ... deduct from any
-- remuneration payable on such termination" the ordinary pay paid for the leave taken beyond the entitlement; (5AA):
-- not more than the ordinary pay for that leave "had it been taken on the termination". No deduction while employed, or
-- for leave not taken in advance.
GIVEN f IS A `Service facts`
      `the leave was taken in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `pay per week of the advance leave` IS A NUMBER
      `weekly ordinary pay at termination` IS A NUMBER
      `remuneration payable on termination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be deducted for` f `advance` `the leave was taken in advance` `paid at` `pay per week of the advance leave` `now` `weekly ordinary pay at termination` `from` `remuneration payable on termination` MEANS
    IF `the services are terminated for` f AND `the leave was taken in advance`
    THEN `the smaller of` (`the smaller of` (`the excess` TIMES `pay per week of the advance leave`) `and` (`the excess` TIMES `weekly ordinary pay at termination`)) `and` (`the larger of` 0 `and` `remuneration payable on termination`)
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the excess` MEANS `the larger of` 0 `and` ((f's `weeks already taken or paid`) MINUS (`the weeks of long service leave for` f))

§§ `s 8(3), s 10, s 10A, s 11 -- records and penalties`

-- s 8(3): the record must be kept "for a period of at least 6 years after the day on which the worker ceases to be
-- employed".
GIVEN `the day I ceased to be employed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the record must be kept until` `the day I ceased to be employed` MEANS `the day I ceased to be employed` `plus months` 72

DECLARE `Penalty answer` IS ONE OF
    `your employer is liable to a penalty of up to 20 penalty units for each contravention, such as not giving or not paying your long service leave or not keeping your record (s 10(1)); you, as a person whose rights are impaired, an inspector or a union secretary may take the proceedings in the Local Court, which may also order the payment due to you, and that order bars a later s 12 claim for it (s 11(1), (2))`
    `your employer is liable to a penalty of up to 20 penalty units for each contravention, such as not giving or not paying your long service leave or not keeping your record (s 10(1)); you, as a person whose rights are impaired, an inspector or a union secretary may take the proceedings in the Local Court, which may also order the payment due to you, and that order bars a later s 12 claim for it (s 11(1), (2)); because your employer is a corporation, a director or manager who knew or ought reasonably to have known of an offence under s 4 or s 8 and did not take all reasonable steps to prevent it is liable to the same maximum (s 10A)`

GIVEN `my employer is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Penalty answer`
`the penalty answer for a corporate employer` `my employer is a corporation` MEANS
    IF `my employer is a corporation`
    THEN `your employer is liable to a penalty of up to 20 penalty units for each contravention, such as not giving or not paying your long service leave or not keeping your record (s 10(1)); you, as a person whose rights are impaired, an inspector or a union secretary may take the proceedings in the Local Court, which may also order the payment due to you, and that order bars a later s 12 claim for it (s 11(1), (2)); because your employer is a corporation, a director or manager who knew or ought reasonably to have known of an offence under s 4 or s 8 and did not take all reasonable steps to prevent it is liable to the same maximum (s 10A)`
    ELSE `your employer is liable to a penalty of up to 20 penalty units for each contravention, such as not giving or not paying your long service leave or not keeping your record (s 10(1)); you, as a person whose rights are impaired, an inspector or a union secretary may take the proceedings in the Local Court, which may also order the payment due to you, and that order bars a later s 12 claim for it (s 11(1), (2))`

§§ `s 12 -- recovering unpaid long service leave pay`

-- s 12(1): the worker may apply to the Local Court or the Industrial Relations Commission in Court Session "for an order
-- directing the employer to pay ... the full amount of any payment which has become due to the worker under this Act at
-- any time during the period of 6 years immediately preceding the date of the application". The six years before an
-- application made on day A run from the same day six years earlier, so a payment due on day D can be recovered by an
-- application made on or before D plus 6 years (fork F12). s 4(9): the personal representative recovers in like manner.
GIVEN `the day the payment became due` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for a payment due on` `the day the payment became due` MEANS `the day the payment became due` `plus months` 72

DECLARE `Recovery party` IS ONE OF `the worker`

DECLARE `Recovery act` IS ONE OF `apply for an order for the payment`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Recovery party` `Recovery act`
`the application must be made within 6 years` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY  `the worker`
    MUST   `apply for an order for the payment`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    LEST   BREACH BY `the worker` BECAUSE "the payment fell due more than 6 years before the application, so s 12 does not reach it"

DECLARE `Recovery answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: the payment fell due within the 6 years before your application (s 12(1))`
    `too late: the payment fell due more than 6 years before your application, so s 12 does not let the court order it (s 12(1))`
    `still in time: you have not applied yet, and an application today would be within 6 years of the day the payment fell due (s 12(1))`
    `too late: you have not applied, and more than 6 years have passed since the payment fell due (s 12(1))`

-- On the stable l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE matches FULFILLED; anything else is the breach. Day 0 is the day the
-- payment fell due. Takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Recovery party` `Recovery act`
      `the day it fell due` IS A DATE
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Recovery answer`
`the recovery deadline` `the rule` `from` `the day it fell due` `applied` `I have applied` `on` `the day I applied` `as of` `today` MEANS
    IF `I have applied`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `apply for an order for the payment` (`the days from` `the day it fell due` `to` `the day I applied`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `in time: the payment fell due within the 6 years before your application (s 12(1))`
         OTHERWISE `too late: the payment fell due more than 6 years before your application, so s 12 does not let the court order it (s 12(1))`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the worker` `apply for an order for the payment` (`the days from` `the day it fell due` `to` `today`)))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still in time: you have not applied yet, and an application today would be within 6 years of the day the payment fell due (s 12(1))`
         OTHERWISE `too late: you have not applied, and more than 6 years have passed since the payment fell due (s 12(1))`

GIVEN `the day it fell due` IS A DATE, `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day I applied` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Recovery answer`
`the recovery answer for a payment due on` `the day it fell due` `applied` `I have applied` `on` `the day I applied` `as of` `today` MEANS
    `the recovery deadline` (`the application must be made within 6 years` (`the days from` `the day it fell due` `to` (`the last day to apply for a payment due on` `the day it fell due`))) `from` `the day it fell due` `applied` `I have applied` `on` `the day I applied` `as of` `today`
